DJ PLAYLIST EDITOR

DJ Playlist Editor — a real-world task using only today's concepts: append(), insert(), remove(), pop(), creating lists, len(), in, repeating menus, while loops, break, comparisons, if / elif / else, variables, input(), and printing. No imports, no tricks.

Solve it individually, then come together as a group to compare approaches. Good luck!

A DJ is lining up tonight's playlist at a lounge on Аба Road. He wants an editor that shows a menu, does what he picks, and comes back to the menu - until he chooses Done.

The menu:

----- PLAYLIST -----
1. Add song to end
2. Add song to top
3. Remove a song
4. Play next song
5. Done

The rules:
- Option 1: ask the song title, add it to the END of the playlist, print: Added to end: SongTitle
- Option 2: ask the song title, add it to the TOP of the playlist (position 1), print: Added to top: SongTitle
- Option 3: ask the title. If it is in the playlist, remove it and print: Removed: SongTitle. If not: Not in the playlist - and back to the menu.
- Option 4: if the playlist has songs, take the FIRST song off and print: Now playing: SongTitle. If it is empty: Playlist is empty.
- Option 5: leave the menu and print the final playlist, numbered, one song per line: 1. SongTitle - or Playlist is empty if nothing is left.

Sample run (after this sequence):

Choose (1-5): 2
Song title: Anthem
Added to top: Anthem
Choose (1-5): 1
Song title: Bounce
Added to end: Bounce
Choose (1-5): 4
Now playing: Anthem
Choose (1-5): 5

1. Bounce

Edge cases to handle: playing next from an empty playlist, removing a song that was never added, adding to top then to end and checking the order is right, Done straight away on an empty playlist, and removing a song from the middle.
